tied to a defined research objective and lot record."}]}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","$4","3",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Compliance notice"}],null,[["$","p","0",{"children":["$","span",null,{"children":"ET10 is supplied for research use only. It is not for human or veterinary use, not for consumption, and statements on this page are reference context rather than medical claims."}]}]],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}],["$","article","research",{"id":"research","className":"content-panel","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-title","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Research"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"panel-body","children":[["$","$4","0",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Reference literature focus"}],null,[["$","p","0",{"children":["$","span",null,{"children":"The LPPEPTIDE knowledge record describes Epithalon / Epitalon as a synthetic Ala-Glu-Asp-Gly tetrapeptide from pineal research, reviewed for telomerase, telomere, melatonin, sleep, circadian, and animal longevity models. Research typically reviews pineal peptide signaling, cellular aging markers, oxidative stress models, and telomere-related literature."}]}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","$4","1",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Study design notes"}],null,[["$","p","0",{"children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Use the LPPeptide product knowledge record, current LPPeptide COA, and internal lab SOP to confirm identity, concentration, and endpoints before this material enters a study. The matched LPPeptide reference specification is 10mg x 10 vials / 50mg x 10 vials."}]}]],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}],["$","article","dosing",{"id":"dosing","className":"content-panel","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-title","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Dosing & Protocol"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"panel-body","children":[["$","$4","0",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"LPPeptide handling reference"}],null,[["$","p","0",{"children":["$","span",null,{"children":"LPPEPTIDE knowledge source: add 2.0 mL bacteriostatic water for 5 mg/mL. Reference amount is once daily 5,000 mcg for 20 days. At 5 mg/mL, 1 U equals 50 mcg."}]}],"$L3f"],"$undefined"]}],"$L40","$L41"]}]]}],"$L42","$L43"],"$L44","$L45",["$L46"],"$L47","$L48"]}]
